cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pynhts, please cite it as below."
title: "pynhts: survey-weight-aware access to US National Household Travel Survey microdata"
version: 0.8.1
date-released: 2026-10-22
license: BSD-3-Clause
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23573454"   # Zenodo concept DOI: always resolves to the latest archived version
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23575312"
    description: "Zenodo archive of version 0.8.1"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sabernaseralavi-60/pynhts"
authors:
  - family-names: Naseralavi
    given-names: Seyed Saber
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5392-910X"
    affiliation: "Department of Civil Engineering, Shahid Bahonar University of Kerman, Kerman, Iran"
keywords: [NHTS, travel survey, transportation, replicate weights, jackknife, Taylor series]
abstract: >-
  Python library that downloads and verifies the 2001, 2009, 2017 and 2022 NHTS public-use files,
  converts them to typed Parquet, merges the tables without silent errors, computes
  design-correct standard errors (jackknife for 2001, 2009 and 2017, Taylor series for 2022) and
  margins of error, compares the waves through validated code crosswalks, and reproduces
  published FHWA tables.
